{"name":"Bramble Bush","hex":"#503629","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bramble","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of many closely related thorny plants in the genus Rubus including the blackberry and likely not including the raspberry proper.","Any thorny shrub."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To pick or collect blackberries from brambles."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bramble"},{"term":"bush","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A woody plant distinguished from a tree by its multiple stems and lower height, being usually less than six metres tall; a horticultural rather than strictly botanical category.","A shrub cut off, or a shrublike branch of a tree."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To branch thickly in the manner of a bush.","To set bushes for; to support with bushes."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bush"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Bramble Bush","blocks":[{"text":"The Bramble Bush is a 1960 American drama film, based on the controversial novel of the same name, directed by Daniel Petrie and starring Richard Burton, Angie Dickinson, Barbara Rush, Jack Carson and James Dunn. It was released by Warner Bros. Pictures."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/af/The-bramble-bush-movieposter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Bramble_Bush","wikidata":"Q7719831"},{"title":"Rubus","blocks":[{"text":"Rubus is a large and diverse genus of flowering plants in the rose family, Rosaceae, subfamily Rosoideae, most commonly known as brambles. Fruits of various species are known as raspberries, blackberries, dewberries, cloudberries, and bristleberries. It is a diverse genus, and estimates of the number of Rubus species vary from 250 to over 1,000, found across all continents except Antarctica."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/-2020-09-23_Blackberrys%2C_Coast_Path%2C_Trimingham.JPG/330px--2020-09-23_Blackberrys%2C_Coast_Path%2C_Trimingham.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rubus","wikidata":"Q602740"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/James_Dunn_and_Richard_Burton_in_%22The_Bramble_Bush%22_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-James_Dunn_and_Richard_Burton_in_%22The_Bramble_Bush%22_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/James_Dunn_and_Richard_Burton_in_%22The_Bramble_Bush%22_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-James_Dunn_and_Richard_Burton_in_%22The_Bramble_Bush%22_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Richard Burton (right) and James Dunn in a publicity still","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJames_Dunn_and_Richard_Burton_in_%22The_Bramble_Bush%22_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Rubus_caesius_fruit_-_Keila.jpg/500px-Rubus_caesius_fruit_-_Keila.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Rubus_caesius_fruit_-_Keila.jpg/1280px-Rubus_caesius_fruit_-_Keila.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Rubus_caesius_fruit_-_Keila.jpg/500px-Rubus_caesius_fruit_-_Keila.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rubus caesius berry","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARubus_caesius_fruit_-_Keila.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Rubus_arcticus3.jpg/500px-Rubus_arcticus3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Rubus_arct